==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
An accusative form of {{m|non|heimr||abode, world, land}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{m|gem-pro|*haimaz}}. Compare {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|hēm}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|hām}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|heim}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌷𐌰𐌹𐌼𐍃}}.

===Adverb===
{{non-adv}}

# [[home]], [[homewards]]
#: ''Flosi var allra manna glaðastr ok beztr '''[[sækja heim#Old Norse|heim]]''' at [[sækja heim#Old Norse|sækja]].''
#:: Flosi was most cheerful of all men and the best to [[visit]].

====Derived terms====
* [[bæta heim fyrir sér]] (to make for one's soul's weal)
* [[bjóða heim]] (to bid one to a feast, ''confer'' '''[[heimboð]]''')
* [[fara heim]] (to return home, to go home)
* [[fara heim á leið]]
* [[sækja heim]] (to visit, to attack somebody)

====Descendants====
* Icelandic: {{l|is|heim}}
* Faroese: {{l|fo|heim}}
* Norwegian: {{l|no|heim}}
** Bokmål: {{l|nb|hjem}}
* Swedish: {{l|sv|hem}}
* Danish: {{l|da|hjem}}

